<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boris Pasternak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boris Pasternak was a Russian poet, novelist and translator, one of the major lyric poets of the twentieth century. His novel Doctor Zhivago, rejected by Soviet publishers, appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1957 and became an international success. When he was awarded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Literature in 1958, an official campaign of vilification forced him to decline it, and he died in disgrace two years later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boris-pasternak.jpg" alt="Boris Pasternak" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Владимир Савостьянов / ТАСС · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boris_Pasternak_1958_photo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
